00:01:08.069 --> 00:01:09.310
the air.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.569
So History of the Faceless Men:

00:01:10.569 --> 00:01:15.149
Their religion came first, the worship of
the Many Faced God. It originated in the Valyrian

00:01:15.149 --> 00:01:19.909
Slave Mines. This is old Valyrian, pre-doom.
The tale goes that a man heard all of the

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:25.149
slaves whispering prayers to different gods
for deliverance from death and decided that

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:29.639
they were all speaking to the same god. Thus
Many Gods with Many faces became one god with

00:01:29.639 --> 00:01:31.810
Many Faces.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.060
That first man gave what they call the “gift
of mercy”, death basically. To the most

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.259
desperate slaves in the mines. Eventually
he gave the gift to their masters and their

00:01:38.259 --> 00:01:42.229
history kind of drops off. It’s rumored
that the order grew to the point that they

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:46.649
were able to influence the Doom in Valyria,
like they were somehow involved in it coming

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:50.639
to pass. Whether they were granted a boon
by the many faced god or they just killed

00:01:50.639 --> 00:01:52.249
anyone capable of stopping it.

00:01:52.249 --> 00:01:53.709
That’s just a rumor though.

00:01:53.709 --> 00:01:57.849
After the Doom they established themselves
as a proper Order in Braavos, their guild’s

00:01:57.849 --> 00:02:02.109
home, their temple is called the House of
Black and White. In terms of where it’s

00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:07.270
located in Braavos specifically. I already
did a Braavos video where I get into a detailed

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.880
map layout of the city. So I’ll add links
for that at the end of this video and in the

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.960
description.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.880
Not all followers of their order become Faceless
Men, that’s a special elite order inside

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.100
the religion. Women are allowed to become
Faceless Men and children too, but it’s

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.390
very rare.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.330
The different names of the Many-Faced god
are based on the region the slaves came from.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:28.270
In Qohor it’s called The Black Goat, in
Yi Ti it’s called the Lion of the Night,

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.770
in the faith of the Seven, it’s called The
Stranger.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:37.770
When I first started getting into the series
I wondered if the same thing was true for

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:42.280
the Faith of The Seven, just because some
of the aspects of the Many Faced God sounded

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:42.640
familiar to the Seven.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.980
I tend to believe it the way the books present
it. The Many Faced God is also one of the

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.650
seven. But not all of the Seven.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:52.370
I know there’s a debate that has continued
on since the books were first published, as

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.650
to whether any of the gods were just different
aspects of the same god. Like the Great Other

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.380
and R’hollor, the Red God being two aspects
of the same power.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.370
I don’t believe that, just because George
RR Martin based those two gods on Zoroastrianism

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:03.730
which states that there is a creator who isn’t
present in the world. He’s represented by

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.370
divine beings and great acts of nature. There
is no evil that is part of him. So Evil comes

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:14.540
from another source, the word in the language
for it translates to “lies” and the forces

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.930
of good try to neutralize the evil. So there’s
this back and forth push pull going on with

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.900
the creator being completely distant from
it in the physical sense.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.440
So For All Intents and purposes, if the Great
Other and R’hollor can be different gods

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.760
it means the other gods can be different gods.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:27.600
It can be a little confusing, but I think
that most of the gods are separate entities.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.260
Not all, but most.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:32.610
As part of the Faceless One’s beliefs, when
they kill someone, they see it as a mercy.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:37.370
They’re releasing someone from the burden
of life. The death of the target is a sacrament

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:42.370
to the many faced god. In their temple they
also allow people to commit assisted suicide

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:43.569
by drinking poison.

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:49.630
When someone wishes to kill themselves the
Faceless Ones provide them with a black cup

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:50.280
of poison.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.600
Some other big rules are that when you enter
the order you forsake your identity and you’re

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.420
only allowed to kill the targets you are hired
to kill. You couldn’t just go out murdering

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.380
anyone you wanted. Unless someone named them
to you like Arya named to Jaquen.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.060
In the House of Black and white there are
many levels going down below the ground. In

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:10.940
the main ground level area there are statues
to over 30 different gods. People can come

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:17.630
in and light candles but this is also the
area where people come in to buy poison if

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.379
they want to kill themselves.

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:21.419
It’s not like a church, they don’t hold
services like you see in the faith of the

00:04:21.419 --> 00:04:26.699
seven. But the preists can assist people when
requested.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:30.060
The priests and acolytes sleep on the first
sub level, then below that is where the servants

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:34.169
sleep, then below that on the 3rd level is
the holy sanctum. It’s where they keep all

00:04:34.169 --> 00:04:37.909
the “faces” they collect. They collect
and preserve the faces of the people that

00:04:37.909 --> 00:04:40.999
come to them to die. And then use those faces
as disguises.

00:04:40.999 --> 00:04:45.099
As part of their training, they master the
ability to use the faces. Like when we saw

00:04:45.099 --> 00:04:47.900
Jaquen change his face at the end of season
2.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.490
Everyone is required to give up their name
when they join the order, but there are several

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:55.659
important figures in the order. There’s
the Kindly Man, the Handsome Man, The Fat

00:04:55.659 --> 00:05:02.659
Fellow, The Stern Face, The Squinter, the
Lordling, the Starved Man, Plague Face, The

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.509
Waif and The Alchemist.

00:05:05.509 --> 00:05:12.080
There’s no telling how the show will treat
these characters so I’ll wait till episodes

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:19.080
air to go into more detail. But I will answer
questions in the comments.

00:05:28.719 --> 00:05:34.569
The price they charge for killing someone
depends on how important the target is. But

00:05:34.569 --> 00:05:40.370
they will kill anyone in the world, King or
Peasant. The price for a King or Queen though

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:44.650
would be astronomical. But they accept more
than just money in exchange for a contract.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.650
You negotiate with them and it could involve
you giving them some non-monetary thing of

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:46.740
high value.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:51.349
They haven’t really done a lot with the
Faceless Ones on the show yet, but as of where

00:05:51.349 --> 00:05:55.279
we are in the books, there have been several
times people hired them.

00:05:55.279 --> 00:05:59.120
In the first book Robert Baratheon’s small
council thinks about hiring a Faceless Man

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:04.979
to kill Daenerys, this was all before the
Dragons were born.

00:06:04.979 --> 00:06:08.819
In Book 2 Arya of course meets Faceless Man
Jaqen H’ghar.

00:06:08.819 --> 00:06:15.309
In Book 3 Arya hears an old woman called the
ghost of high heart telling a story to the

00:06:15.309 --> 00:06:17.449
brotherhood without banners about a dream
she had. She said she saw a man without a

00:06:17.449 --> 00:06:21.360
face, waiting on a bridge that swayed and
swung.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.279
The show didn’t do this, but remember at
the end of season 2 when Jaqen left Arya,

00:06:25.279 --> 00:06:28.849
he gave her the Braavosi coin and taught her
that she could give the coin to any Braavosi

00:06:28.849 --> 00:06:33.400
ship captain and say the words Valar Morghulis
and they’d take her to Braavos for free.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.659
It’s like Willy Wonka’s Golden Ticket
to WTF. There’s a certain excitement to

00:06:36.659 --> 00:06:42.800
it as you see Arya’s face in the season
4 finale on the boat. But it’s also very

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:49.800
sinister. Valar Morhulis, is High Valyrian
for All Men Must Die. The formal response

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.680
is Valar Dohaeris, “All Men Must Serve”.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:56.080
I like to think of the exchange as being “All
Men Must Serve Death”, but that’s just

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.610
my interpretation.
